\tag{fdip}
\title{Refinement of finite calculi}
\date{2026-11-12}

\p{The objects are the finite calculi already constructed. A morphism
is a relabeling, a subdivision, or a coarse-graining, and it
commutes with the coboundary.}

\p{On the dyadic towers of the cycle and the square torus, the dual
of subdivision commutes with the coboundary. Stokes and the
vanishing of #{d^2} commute with it. The inverse limit is a module
of compatible cell functions. It is not a module of smooth forms,
and the tower is a pro-object among finite calculi.}

\p{The cup product and the unweighted adjoint do not commute with
subdivision. A declared factor of two matches the massless
Dirichlet form on the affine extensions of the cycle. The massive
retained shape does not.}

